        "department": "CSE",
        "description": "Discrete mathematics is one of the most fundamental courses in computer science, crucial for developing the mathematical maturity required across a wide range of areas in the field. This course is designed to strengthen students\u2019 logical reasoning and analytical thinking, equipping them with the ability to understand and construct rigorous mathematical proofs. It introduces and explores foundational mathematical structures such as sets, functions, relations, and graphs\u2014concepts that are ubiquitous across algorithms, data structures, theory of computation, databases, and more. Additionally, the course nurtures combinatorial thinking and problem-solving strategies, crucial for solving computational problems.",
